  "term": "group difference",
  "definition": "A group difference is a measured distinction between two or more groups on a variable being studied. In this packet, it refers to comparing lesbian/gay and bisexual students on factors such as identity centrality, identity uncertainty, interpersonal discrimination, and depressive symptoms to see whether the groups differ.",
